I was googling for calcium fluoride and found a page that claims that Irish 
moss contains it. (The page shows blank - probably a CSS bug - so I'm reading 
the source.) Irish moss is not moss, or even lichen (which I distinguish by 
calling moss {clikyspa}), but seaweed. So I thought of calling it {gailge 
alga}. Can you think of a better name? The scientific name is Chondrus 
crispus.

